# 🎉 Python Fun Fact

Many data-processing scripts use dictionary-based CSV handling because named columns make code easier to understand, especially when files contain many fields.

---

# 🔄 Quick Recap

- `csv.DictReader()` returns each row as a dictionary.
- `csv.DictWriter()` writes dictionaries to CSV files.
- Dictionary keys match the column headers.
- Named fields improve readability and reduce indexing errors.

